00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:10.400
SPEAKER: reCAPTCHA Enterprise
helps protect your website

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.980
from fraudulent activity,
spam, and abuse.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.070
reCAPTCHA Enterprise
helps protect your website

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.490
by stopping malicious actions,
such as fraudulent transactions

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.820
and false posts, while allowing
legitimate users to interact

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.238
with your website, and
without interruption.

00:00:25.238 --> 00:00:26.780
reCAPTCHA has been
defending millions

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.780
of sites for almost a decade,
and the reCAPTCHA Enterprise

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.360
service builds on this
technology with capabilities

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.950
such as two-factor
authentication

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.020
and mobile support,
designed specifically

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.407
for enterprise
security concerns.

00:00:38.407 --> 00:00:40.490
There are several threats
that can target your web

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:43.590
applications as a result of
malicious web automation.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.482
Credential stuffing
is one of them,

00:00:45.482 --> 00:00:47.690
and we'll take a look at
how reCAPTCHA Enterprise can

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.360
stop credential stuffing.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.770
Credential stuffing is when
there are mass login attempts

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.980
used to verify the validity of
stolen user name and password

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.360
pairs.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.340
If we go to the reCAPTCHA
Enterprise Admin

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.610
portal in Google
Cloud platform, we

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:03.050
are able to see the response
of a legitimate action

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:06.440
from a real user due to
a couple of key metrics.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.270
Number of requests
is a simple count

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:09.680
of how many
assessments have been

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.050
made with a particular
reCAPTCHA key.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.150
Every time the user hits
a page that the customer

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:17.630
has instrumented, the
count should go up by one.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:20.600
These assessments are scored
and we give three color-coded

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.030
buckets to help visualize this--

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.640
low risk, medium
risk, high risk.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.040
Score distribution
returns a score

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.470
based on interactions
with your websites,

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:36.700
with 1.0 being a likely good
interaction, and 0.0 being

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.830
a likely abusive action.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.230
reCAPTCHA Enterprise
calculates this risk score

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:43.870
by using machine learning
models based on user behavior

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.550
patterns.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:48.580
Top 10 actions is a view
of the number of requests,

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.680
but instead of
separated by date,

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.690
they're separated by action.

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:54.310
Actions are defined
by the user when

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:56.110
they instrument their site.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:58.810
Particularly, to be able to
analyze this data separately

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:00.890
from other actions.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:03.160
For example, you might
want to tell apart

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:06.960
the traffic from the home page
rather than the payment page.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.759
Top 10 risky actions is when
actions are being sorted

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:13.330
by percentage of risky traffic.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:14.940
Congratulations.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.960
You successfully used
reCAPTCHA Enterprise

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.360
to help protect your business
from credential stuffing

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.670
and other web-based attacks.

